Interview with the Vampire is a 1994 American gothic horror film directed by Neil Jordan and written by
Anne Rice, based on her 1976 novel of the same name, and starring Tom Cruise and Brad Pitt.

11
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
It focuses on Lestat (Cruise) and Louis (Pitt), beginning with
Louis' transformation into a vampire by Lestat in 1791.

12
01:07:05,454 --> 01:07:11,454
The film chronicles their time together, and their turning of
young Claudia (Kirsten Dunst) into a vampire.

13
01:12:40,909 --> 01:12:46,909
The narrative is framed by a modern-day interview, in which Louis tells
his story to a San Francisco reporter (Christian Slater).

14
01:18:16,363 --> 01:18:22,363
The supporting cast features Antonio Banderas and Stephen Rea.

15
01:23:51,818 --> 01:23:57,818
The film was released by Warner Bros.

16
01:29:27,272 --> 01:29:33,272
on November 11, 1994 to generally positive reviews and was a commercial
success, grossing $223.7 million against a $60 million budget.

17
01:35:02,727 --> 01:35:08,727
It received two Academy Award nominations for Best
Art Direction and Best Original Score.

18
01:40:38,181 --> 01:40:44,181
Kirsten Dunst was additionally nominated for a Golden Globe for
Best Supporting Actress for her role in the film.

19
01:46:13,636 --> 01:46:19,636
